{
  "voice": "af_heart",
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "cold",
      "title": "Cold open",
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 10.0,
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "c1",
          "text": "Hundreds of notifications a day.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 1.804
        },
        {
          "id": "c2",
          "text": "A text that says his bank account is blocked.",
          "start": 2.831,
          "end": 5.071
        },
        {
          "id": "c3",
          "text": "And it's exam week.",
          "start": 6.097,
          "end": 7.126
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "title",
      "title": "Title",
      "start": 10.0,
      "end": 18.0,
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "t1",
          "text": "His phone knew all of it.",
          "start": 10.0,
          "end": 11.146
        },
        {
          "id": "t2",
          "text": "His AI agent knew none of it.",
          "start": 11.587,
          "end": 13.133
        },
        {
          "id": "t3",
          "text": "Until now.",
          "start": 14.235,
          "end": 14.916
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "problem",
      "title": "The problem",
      "start": 18.0,
      "end": 50.0,
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "p1",
          "text": "Meet Arpit. A final-year student in Hamirpur, Himachal Pradesh.",
          "start": 18.0,
          "end": 21.981
        },
        {
          "id": "p2",
          "text": "Everything in his life lands on his phone first.",
          "start": 22.609,
          "end": 25.16
        },
        {
          "id": "p3",
          "text": "In October, India made over twenty-five billion UPI payments.",
          "start": 25.997,
          "end": 29.985
        },
        {
          "id": "p4",
          "text": "His bank texts him for every one.",
          "start": 30.403,
          "end": 32.024
        },
        {
          "id": "p5",
          "text": "The average Indian sees thirteen scam messages a day.",
          "start": 32.861,
          "end": 36.067
        },
        {
          "id": "p6",
          "text": "And since twenty twenty-one, Indians have reported over fifty-five thousand crore rupees in cyber fraud.",
          "start": 36.904,
          "end": 42.965
        },
        {
          "id": "p7",
          "text": "His agent lives on his laptop, a foot away.",
          "start": 44.011,
          "end": 46.542
        },
        {
          "id": "p8",
          "text": "And it can't see any of it.",
          "start": 46.961,
          "end": 48.117
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "turn",
      "title": "The painkiller",
      "start": 50.0,
      "end": 70.0,
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "k1",
          "text": "So Arpit built the fix. Phone Senses.",
          "start": 50.0,
          "end": 52.403
        },
        {
          "id": "k2",
          "text": "A Hermes plugin that gives his agent the senses of his own phone.",
          "start": 53.443,
          "end": 57.002
        },
        {
          "id": "k3",
          "text": "No screen tapping. It talks to Android directly, through Termux.",
          "start": 57.782,
          "end": 61.62
        },
        {
          "id": "k4",
          "text": "And it always asks before it touches anything.",
          "start": 62.4,
          "end": 64.702
        },
        {
          "id": "k5",
          "text": "Here's his real day, on his real phone.",
          "start": 65.742,
          "end": 67.92
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "walk",
      "title": "Walkthrough",
      "start": 70.0,
      "end": 163.6,
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "w1",
          "text": "Morning. One question: give me my phone brief.",
          "start": 70.0,
          "end": 72.777
        },
        {
          "id": "w2",
          "text": "Hermes reads what his phone sees, and puts the scam text right at the top.",
          "start": 73.584,
          "end": 77.64
        },
        {
          "id": "w3",
          "text": "One-time codes stay hidden. When Hermes tried to reveal one, it had to ask. Nobody said yes, so it stayed hidden.",
          "start": 79.253,
          "end": 86.034
        },
        {
          "id": "w4",
          "text": "Where did his money go? Every bank SMS, sorted by category.",
          "start": 88.05,
          "end": 91.706
        },
        {
          "id": "w5",
          "text": "And every rupee that came in by UPI.",
          "start": 92.512,
          "end": 94.774
        },
        {
          "id": "w6",
          "text": "Bills before they're late, and subscriptions, added up for the month.",
          "start": 96.388,
          "end": 99.76
        },
        {
          "id": "w7",
          "text": "Then the text that almost got him. Hermes flags it, and shows why.",
          "start": 101.776,
          "end": 105.448
        },
        {
          "id": "w8",
          "text": "Text Mom: I'll call you after the exam.",
          "start": 107.465,
          "end": 109.717
        },
        {
          "id": "w9",
          "text": "Hermes stops, and shows the exact words.",
          "start": 110.927,
          "end": 113.261
        },
        {
          "id": "w10",
          "text": "Allow once. It goes from his own SIM.",
          "start": 114.471,
          "end": 116.463
        },
        {
          "id": "w11",
          "text": "One more text? He changes his mind. Deny. Nothing is sent, and Hermes doesn't try again.",
          "start": 118.48,
          "end": 124.079
        },
        {
          "id": "w16",
          "text": "Then a stranger calls about his bank account, and asks him to install AnyDesk. Hermes connects the dots, and the phone warns him out loud.",
          "start": 126.096,
          "end": 134.18
        },
        {
          "id": "w12",
          "text": "A watch rule catches the delivery text, just once.",
          "start": 143.68,
          "end": 146.478
        },
        {
          "id": "w13",
          "text": "Battery under twenty? He'll get a heads-up.",
          "start": 147.687,
          "end": 149.693
        },
        {
          "id": "w14",
          "text": "That night, the phone is gone. Under the bed.",
          "start": 151.709,
          "end": 153.804
        },
        {
          "id": "w15",
          "text": "One line to Hermes. It rings, speaks, vibrates and flashes.",
          "start": 155.014,
          "end": 158.761
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "hood",
      "title": "Under the hood",
      "start": 163.6,
      "end": 183.6,
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "h1",
          "text": "Follow one real request: what's my battery?",
          "start": 163.6,
          "end": 166.075
        },
        {
          "id": "h2",
          "text": "The approval hook checks it first. A read passes.",
          "start": 166.542,
          "end": 169.393
        },
        {
          "id": "h3",
          "text": "The request is signed with a secret that's never sent.",
          "start": 169.86,
          "end": 172.767
        },
        {
          "id": "h4",
          "text": "A one-time nonce stops anyone replaying it.",
          "start": 173.078,
          "end": 175.795
        },
        {
          "id": "h5",
          "text": "In Termux, a tiny helper asks Android directly.",
          "start": 176.262,
          "end": 179.41
        },
        {
          "id": "h6",
          "text": "And the answer is back in about a second and a half.",
          "start": 179.721,
          "end": 182.355
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "impact",
      "title": "Impact",
      "start": 183.6,
      "end": 203.6,
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "i1",
          "text": "Before: hundreds of notifications, and an agent that couldn't see them.",
          "start": 183.6,
          "end": 187.429
        },
        {
          "id": "i2",
          "text": "Now: one question, and Hermes knows his whole day.",
          "start": 187.993,
          "end": 190.916
        },
        {
          "id": "i3",
          "text": "It reads the phone itself, not pictures of the screen.",
          "start": 191.667,
          "end": 194.487
        },
        {
          "id": "i4",
          "text": "Texts, calls, photos and codes: all four ask him first.",
          "start": 195.05,
          "end": 198.527
        },
        {
          "id": "i5",
          "text": "Codes stay hidden. The plugin talks only to his phone.",
          "start": 199.09,
          "end": 202.098
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "outro",
      "title": "Outro",
      "start": 203.6,
      "end": 218.6,
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "o1",
          "text": "Phone Senses. Your phone's senses, for Hermes.",
          "start": 203.6,
          "end": 206.23
        },
        {
          "id": "o2",
          "text": "And it still asks before it touches anything.",
          "start": 206.882,
          "end": 208.973
        },
        {
          "id": "o3",
          "text": "Built by Arpit Singh, in Hamirpur. Open source, for Hermes Agent.",
          "start": 209.789,
          "end": 213.944
        },
        {
          "id": "o4",
          "text": "Try it tonight. Link below.",
          "start": 214.596,
          "end": 216.154
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "duration": 218.6
}